{"label":"1A","direction":"against","claim":"At Rush the 6000 S4 lane costs only about 1.9-2.0x the X 25B lane per Gb, far below the ~3.4x gap in Illumina's reported revenue per Gb.","detail":"Rush June 2026: 25B lane (930 Gb) is $4,200 / $4,620, which is $4.52 / $4.97 per Gb. The S4 2x150 lane is $6,615 / $6,945.75; at the 750 Gb per lane Calgary lists for an S4 lane, that is $8.82 / $9.26 per Gb. Ratio = 8.82/4.52 = 1.95x internal and 9.26/4.97 = 1.86x external. Rush prices both near list, so the core gap understates what large-volume customers see.","url":"https://www.rushu.rush.edu/sites/default/files/2026-06/GMCF%20Pricing%20June%202026.pdf","date":"2026-06-15","source_name":"Rush University GMCF June 2026 sheet","source_type":"price_list","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Rush's S4 lane price and the computed per-Gb ratio are new; the probe flagged this but had not resolved the unit (per lane) or computed it."},
